  "verbalization": "Trigohowilol G is implicated in the regulation of Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein through multiple pathways. The evidence suggests that Trigohowilol G acts as a target of two distinct compounds, DOHH-2 and Porsapogenin 7, both of which are themselves targets of the Macrophage-expressed gene 1 protein. This indicates a potential mechanism where Trigohowilol G may influence the expression or activity of the gene through interactions with these compounds. The presence of a direct target relationship between Trigohowilol G and the gene, as well as the involvement of other compounds in the pathway, suggests a possible role in modulating macrophage function. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the regulatory network, where Trigohowilol G may exert its effects through indirect interactions, possibly via the compounds it targets. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Trigohowilol G and the gene, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
